#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# riemann_r

#% text
# `riemann_r(x)` gives Riemann's approximation `R(x)` to the number of primes up to `x`, by Gram's series `1 + sum((ln x)^k/(k k! zeta(k + 1)))`; evaluated for inexact `x` (real or complex, at the precision of `x`), `riemann_r(1)` is 1.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
riemann_r(1000.)
#% output
#= 168.35944628116727

#% cell
riemann_r([2., 3., 4.])
#% output
#= [1.541009016187132, 2.0046766483089256, 2.426657752706807]

#% cell
riemann_r(1.5 + sqrt(-1))
#% output
#= 1.3324367394020404 + 0.5220926889611722im

#% cell
prime_pi(1000)
#% output
#= 168

